    "bosom": {
      "word": "BOSOM",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "The breast of a human being; the part, between the arms, to which anything is pressed when embraced by them. You must prepare your bosom for his knife. Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The breast, considered as the seat of the passions, affections, and operations of the mind; consciousness; se Tut, I am in their bosoms, and I know Wherefore they do it. Shak. If I covered my transgressions as Adam, by hiding my iniquity in my bosom. Job xxxi. 33.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Embrace; loving or affectionate inclosure; fold. Within the bosom of that church. Hooker.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Any thing or place resembling the breast; a supporting surface; an inner recess; the interior; as, the bosom of the earth. \"The bosom of the ocean.\" Addison.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The part of the dress worn upon the breast; an article, or a portion of an article, of dress to be worn upon the breast; as, the bosom of a shirt; a linen bosom. He put his hand into his bosom: and when he took it out, behold, his hand was leprous as snow. Ex. iv. 6.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Inclination; desire. [Obs.] Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A depression round the eye of a millstone. Knight.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Of or pertaining to the bosom.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "Intimate; confidential; familiar; trusted; cherished; beloved; as, a bosom friend.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "To inclose or carry in the bosom; to keep with care; to take to heart; to cherish. Bosom up my counsel, You'll find it wholesome. Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To conceal; to hide from view; to embosom. To happy convents bosomed deep in vines. Pope.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
