    "boss": {
      "word": "BOSS",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "Any protuberant part; a round, swelling part or body; a knoblike process; as, a boss of wood.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A protuberant ornament on any work, either of different material from that of the work or of the same, as upon a buckler or bridle; a stud; a knob; the central projection of a shield. See Umbilicus.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Arch.)",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A projecting ornament placed at the intersection of the ribs of ceilings, whether vaulted or flat, and in other situations.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Etym: [Cf. D. bus box, Dan. bösse.]",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A wooden vessel for the mortar used in tiling or masonry, hung by a hook from the laths, or from the rounds of a ladder. Gwilt.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Mech.) (a) The enlarged part of a shaft, on which a wheel is keyed, or at the end, where it is coupled to another. (b) A swage or die used for shaping metals.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A head or reservoir of water. [Obs.]",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "To ornament with bosses; to stud.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "A master workman or superintendent; a director or manager; a political dictator. [Slang, U. S.]",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        }
      ],
